From f0331556515d9c742bb2f4226e0afbf208d6295b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:47:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/31] PCI: zh: clear pcie->phy when devm_phy_get() fails

zhihe_pcie_phy_init() leaves pcie->phy holding the ERR_PTR when
devm_phy_get() fails. If host init then fails -- which it always does when
the PHY node is disabled in DT, as on boards that don't use PCIe -- the
probe error path calls zhihe_pcie_phy_deinit() -> phy_exit(pcie->phy).
phy_exit() only NULL-checks its argument, so the ERR_PTR is dereferenced
and the kernel oopses in the udev coldplug worker at every boot:

  zh-pcie b800000.pcie: Failed to initialize host
  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffffffffffffff7b
  epc : phy_exit+0x12/0xcc
   ra : zhihe_pcie_probe+0x1aa/0xb4a [pcie_zh]

Clear pcie->phy to NULL on the failed get so the deinit path is a no-op.

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-zh.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-zh.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-zh.c
index 1e8804db2d23f..bc595e070be67 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-zh.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-zh.c
@@ -178,9 +178,18 @@ static int __maybe_unused zhihe_pcie_phy_init(struct zhihe_pcie *pcie)
 	int ret;
 
 	pcie->phy = devm_phy_get(dev, "pcie-phy");
-	if (IS_ERR(pcie->phy))
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(pcie->phy),
-				     "missing PHY\n");
+	if (IS_ERR(pcie->phy)) {
+		ret = dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(pcie->phy),
+				    "missing PHY\n");
+		/*
+		 * Clear the ERR_PTR: the probe error path calls
+		 * zhihe_pcie_phy_deinit() -> phy_exit(pcie->phy), and
+		 * phy_exit() only NULL-checks -- an ERR_PTR here oopses
+		 * (seen when the PHY node is disabled in DT).
+		 */
+		pcie->phy = NULL;
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	ret = phy_init(pcie->phy);
 	if (ret)
